<article class="env-lemma" id="0FPF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0FPF">Lemma <span data-tag="0FPF">20.52.1</span>.</a> Let $(X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$ be a ringed space. Set $R = \Gamma (X, \mathcal{O}_ X)$. The category of $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules which are summands of finite free $\mathcal{O}_ X$-modules is equivalent to the category of finite projective $R$-modules. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Observe that a finite projective $R$-module is the same thing as a summand of a finite free $R$-module. The equivalence is given by the functor $\mathcal{E} \mapsto \Gamma (X, \mathcal{E})$. The inverse functor is given by the construction of Modules, Lemma <a href="/tag/01BH" data-tag="01BH">17.10.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>